# Content is a function of distDir, and this repo runs two distDir values by
# design (.next-dev under the dev-server rule, .next under next build). No
# committed copy of next-env.d.ts can be correct for both, so tracking it
# means fighting the generator on every run. next dev / next build regenerate
# it; nothing in the gate list reads it — confirmed with a direct
# `npx tsc --noEmit` in the fresh-clone shape (file absent, .next-dev absent,
# no turbo cache in the loop).
apps/playground/next-env.d.ts

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
# `**/` prefix is load-bearing, not decorative — cycle 003 §15.5. A pattern
# containing a `/` is root-anchored by git, so the unprefixed form matched
# only `*-snapshots/` sitting one level deep, which is where a
# `{testFilePath}`-only `snapshotPathTemplate` token bug used to land them.
# Now that baselines nest under `tests/e2e/` (`playwright.config.ts`), the
# unprefixed pattern would silently stop ignoring `-actual`/`-diff` files at
# that depth. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` at both depths; the
# committed baseline itself (no `-actual`/`-diff` suffix) still stays
# trackable either way, which is the whole point of committing baselines.
**/*-snapshots/*-actual.png
**/*-snapshots/*-diff.png

